{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340922",
      "title": "Controlling Data Caching",
      "lectureOrder": 186,
      "videoOrder": 172,
      "sourceHash": "0b667a406ddb0d14f6940b8e01e674ad5cfef1c931c0ff4433557b95d650b9c7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 2.55,
          "en": "So you can control caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.55,
          "end": 5.82,
          "en": "with help of those fetch function settings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.82,
          "end": 7.71,
          "en": "You can alternatively",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.71,
          "end": 10.59,
          "en": "also add some file-wide settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.59,
          "end": 13.38,
          "en": "in case you had multiple components in that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.38,
          "end": 16.47,
          "en": "that would maybe all send fetch requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.47,
          "end": 17.88,
          "en": "Instead of then configuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.88,
          "end": 20.85,
          "en": "all those requests manually step by step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.85,
          "end": 23.28,
          "en": "you could set up a configuration for the entire file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.28,
          "end": 25.8,
          "en": "which would then be used for all the requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.8,
          "end": 28.83,
          "en": "sent from anywhere in that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.83,
          "end": 32.07,
          "en": "And you do that with help of two special constants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.07,
          "end": 35.73,
          "en": "you can add to your NextJS files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.73,
          "end": 40.26,
          "en": "The first constant is the revalidate constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.26,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "This constant serves the same purpose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 45.66,
          "en": "as the revalidate setting on the fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.66,
          "end": 48.33,
          "en": "I showed you a couple of seconds ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.33,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "You can set it to a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 51.66,
          "en": "and that will be the number of seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.66,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "for which data will be cached and reused",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 56.73,
          "en": "until a new request will be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.73,
          "end": 59.67,
          "en": "Now for NextJS to pick up that constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.67,
          "end": 61.95,
          "en": "you also must export it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.95,
          "end": 64.65,
          "en": "and this must be named revalidate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 64.65,
          "end": 69.51,
          "en": "because NextJS will explicitly look for this name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.51,
          "end": 70.86,
          "en": "So with that added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.86,
          "end": 73.17,
          "en": "even if I don't set it on the fetch function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.17,
          "end": 75.93,
          "en": "I'll get this same behavior as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.93,
          "end": 77.34,
          "en": "I got some logs here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.34,
          "end": 79.95,
          "en": "and now if I hammer the refresh button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.95,
          "end": 81.53999999999999,
          "en": "which I am doing right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 81.53999999999999,
          "end": 85.41,
          "en": "you see only one new request was sent to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 85.41,
          "end": 87.78,
          "en": "and then the cached data was reused",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 87.78,
          "end": 89.82,
          "en": "because most of those requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 89.82,
          "end": 92.34,
          "en": "were within that five-second timeframe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 92.34,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "after fetching new data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 97.95,
          "en": "So that's one way of setting this up file-wide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 97.95,
          "end": 101.03999999999999,
          "en": "Now you can also set up that other setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.03999999999999,
          "end": 104.28,
          "en": "where you avoid caching all together file-wide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 104.28,
          "end": 106.05,
          "en": "if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 106.05,
          "end": 110.1,
          "en": "Because you can also export a constant called dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.1,
          "end": 113.88300000000001,
          "en": "which is another reserved name NextJS will be looking for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 114.93,
          "end": 118.89,
          "en": "This dynamic constant takes various values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.89,
          "end": 122.16,
          "en": "The default is auto and doesn't have to be set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.16,
          "end": 125.46,
          "en": "Alternatively, you can set this to force dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 125.46,
          "end": 126.99,
          "en": "which is essentially the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126.99,
          "end": 130.38,
          "en": "as if you set the cache setting on a fetch request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.38,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "to no store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "Because force dynamic tells NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 138.78,
          "en": "to always re-fetch all the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 138.78,
          "end": 141.03300000000002,
          "en": "that's needed anywhere in that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 141.96,
          "end": 143.25,
          "en": "which is exactly the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 143.25,
          "end": 145.38,
          "en": "this cache no store setting did,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 145.38,
          "end": 147.72,
          "en": "now just applied to all requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 147.72,
          "end": 150.45,
          "en": "sent from anywhere in that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 150.45,
          "end": 152.19,
          "en": "With that setting added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 152.19,
          "end": 154.17000000000002,
          "en": "if I open that backend log again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 154.17000000000002,
          "end": 157.53,
          "en": "and I hammer that refresh shortcut here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 157.53,
          "end": 160.47,
          "en": "you'll see that a bunch of new log messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 160.47,
          "end": 162.06,
          "en": "are output here on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 162.06,
          "end": 164.34300000000002,
          "en": "because now indeed no data is cached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 165.6,
          "end": 170.6,
          "en": "You could also set this to force static to force caching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 170.67000000000002,
          "end": 173.97,
          "en": "but this would then really never fetch any new data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 173.97,
          "end": 176.673,
          "en": "which might often not be what you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 177.6,
          "end": 179.49,
          "en": "But force dynamic would be another way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 179.49,
          "end": 181.53,
          "en": "of avoiding caching altogether.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 181.53,
          "end": 182.79,
          "en": "It's not what I'll do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 182.79,
          "end": 186.27,
          "en": "but it is definitely a setting you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 186.27,
          "end": 189.9,
          "en": "And then, there is one last way of making sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 189.9,
          "end": 192.93,
          "en": "that the data here is not cached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 192.93,
          "end": 195.24,
          "en": "and that's a special function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 195.24,
          "end": 199.26,
          "en": "you can import from next cache,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 199.26,
          "end": 203.133,
          "en": "so from this cache sub-package of the next framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 204.09,
          "end": 208.14,
          "en": "And that's the unstable no store function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 208.14,
          "end": 211.2,
          "en": "though at the point of time where you are watching this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 215.07,
          "en": "the unstable prefix might no longer be there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 215.07,
          "end": 218.28,
          "en": "So if you don't find a unstable no store function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 218.28,
          "end": 220.62,
          "en": "try just no store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 220.62,
          "end": 223.98,
          "en": "Because indeed this is a relatively new function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 223.98,
          "end": 228.09,
          "en": "which is recommended to be used over using this dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 228.09,
          "end": 230.22,
          "en": "force dynamic setting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 230.22,
          "end": 231.6,
          "en": "So instead of using that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 231.6,
          "end": 233.94,
          "en": "NextJS recommends using that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 233.94,
          "end": 236.79,
          "en": "But at the point of time where I'm recording this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 236.79,
          "end": 239.37,
          "en": "this function is not marked as stable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 239.37,
          "end": 242.733,
          "en": "and ready for production yet, hence the prefix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 243.63,
          "end": 245.37,
          "en": "But the idea behind this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 245.37,
          "end": 248.85,
          "en": "is that you simply call it inside of the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 248.85,
          "end": 252.42,
          "en": "where you wanna make sure that data is not cached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 252.42,
          "end": 254.28,
          "en": "So you would then get the same effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 254.28,
          "end": 258.39,
          "en": "as if you set this dynamic constant to force dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 258.39,
          "end": 260.88,
          "en": "but you would now get this effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 260.88,
          "end": 262.77,
          "en": "just inside of this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 262.77,
          "end": 265.74,
          "en": "but in that component for all the requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 265.74,
          "end": 268.353,
          "en": "that might be sent to any data sources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 269.67,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "So if you had multiple components in the same page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 275.46,
          "en": "and you wanna cache data in some components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 275.46,
          "end": 277.17,
          "en": "but not all components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 277.17,
          "end": 281.34000000000003,
          "en": "you might not wanna set up a file-wide cache setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 281.34000000000003,
          "end": 283.56,
          "en": "And then, you can instead use this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 283.56,
          "end": 287.07,
          "en": "to just disable caching for one specific component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 287.07,
          "end": 290.43,
          "en": "That's what unstable no store does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 290.43,
          "end": 293.73,
          "en": "And therefore here again, if I restart that backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 293.73,
          "end": 296.28,
          "en": "and I hammer that refresh button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 296.28,
          "end": 298.17,
          "en": "or refresh shortcut,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 298.17,
          "end": 299.76,
          "en": "you see a bunch of logs here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 299.76,
          "end": 303.003,
          "en": "because I disabled caching for this page component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 304.11,
          "end": 308.4,
          "en": "So that's another function in this case you should know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 308.4,
          "end": 310.71,
          "en": "And these are all different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 310.71,
          "end": 314.4,
          "en": "of managing and disabling that data cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 314.4,
          "end": 317.82,
          "en": "or of controlling that data cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 317.82,
          "end": 320.01,
          "en": "It's up to you which approach you want to use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 320.01,
          "end": 321.69,
          "en": "you saw their differences,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 321.69,
          "end": 324.12,
          "en": "and therefore it really just comes down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 324.12,
          "end": 325.803,
          "en": "to your exact use case.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
